# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sched-1 window (the scheduler-side levers; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sched-1 (with the branch tp4/agent-turns merged: see ORDER.txt) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-sched-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the
# same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix-gate jobs (T0-T3, S1) do not forward the checkpoint (c2_serving_job.MODEL_ACTIONS): they run the base
# weights, which the tier's mechanics (what is spilled, restored and counted) do not depend on.
# LE1 (ATTRIBUTION, the admission lever alone): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-lean, the approved profile with the gate marker and
# QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEAN=1, the tests of C1, on Swift. ESTIMATE (docs/tp4-sched-1.md section 4): 541 ms (p50) of a returning turn's engine build become about 255 ms (the
# readback after a slot's first adoption only, about 145; the backstop reading reused, about 70; no "dram after engine" line, about 70, outside the sticky line's own
# clock). READ: sched_report.py against C1 or C2 (the nearer control): the rebind p50 and p90 and the lean split A / B / C, the readbacks skipped (all but the first of each
# slot), the backstop reuses (every admission with the room), the "dram after engine" lines (one per cold build only); the answers EQUAL to the control's. TIMED: the ARC
# runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py
# --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=...
# weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window's W0 built;
# this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1,
# scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A
# rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): 50 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-lean
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,agent_turns,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
